<iscontent type="text/html" charset="UTF-8" compact="true"/>
<iscomment>
    This is the footer for all pages. Be careful caching it if it contains
    user dependent information. Cache its elements instead if necessary (do not forget
    to change the isinclude into a pipeline include for that).
</iscomment>
<isinclude template="util/modules"/>

<footer>
    <div class="footer-container">
        <div class="footer-item">
            <isslot id="footer-column" description="Content in column 1 of the Footer" context="global" />
        </div>
        <div class="footer-item">
            <iscontentasset aid="footer-account"/>
        </div>
        <div class="footer-item">
            <iscontentasset aid="footer-support"/>
        </div>
        <div class="footer-item">
            <iscontentasset aid="footer-about"/>
        </div>
    </div>
</footer>

<iscontentasset aid="footer-copy"/>

<iscomment>
    Customer registration can happen everywhere in the page flow. As special tag in the pdict
    is indicating it. So we have to check on every page, if we have to report this event for
    the reporting engine.
</iscomment>
<isinclude template="util/reporting/ReportUserRegistration.isml"/>

<isinclude template="components/footer/footer_UI"/>

<iscomment>
    ReachFive (Purse Identity) override — CA-7092.

    In simple words: this one line is what actually turns ReachFive on for the page.
    On SFRA, the storefront's own footer already does this; SiteGenesis's footer never
    did, so without it ReachFive's login/social-login SDK never loads anywhere on this
    site, no matter how the ReachFive site preferences are configured.

    This is everything else from the original SiteGenesis footer.isml, unchanged, plus
    this one addition at the end.
</iscomment>
<!-- CA-7092-FOOTER-OVERRIDE-ACTIVE: if you can see this comment in View Page Source,
     this override file IS being used; if the ReachFive script still doesn't appear
     right after it, the problem is inside the hook call below, not the override
     itself. If you can't even find this comment, the override isn't being picked up
     at all (cartridge path / deployment issue). -->
${dw.system.HookMgr.callHook('app.template.afterFooter', 'afterFooter', pdict) || ''}
